{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/540552-apple-of-discord","id":540552,"title":"Apple of Discord","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-04T21:33:17-07:00","id":540552,"title":"Apple of Discord","content":"This Embed has come up in game a few times now. I understand it better now due to the comments on another thread (MacGuffin-maker, and &quot;Helen of Troy&quot; and &quot;There's Something About Mary&quot; references). However, the Exceptional Success is still causing some issues. Also, it's the only power in Demon that uses Integrity as the resistance roll. So I have two questions:<br /> <br /> <br /> 1. Is the Exceptional Success result really intended/expected to cause a riot upon usage (literal, like dropping Inits as people pull out gun/fang/claw) ? Otherwise how exactly is &quot;must immediately acquire&quot; interpreted?<br /> <br /> 2. Using Integrity as the Resistance implies non-Mortals are not affected by this power at all (Demons do not have Integrity or any analogous stat, Vampires' Humanity is similar but represents something very different, and Werewolves' Harmony also doesn't map to Integrity in any way whatsoever). Is that how others interpret it, is that the intended implication, or do most just throw whatever Integrity-replacement in that roll (which makes no sense for Demons' Cover rating)?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T23:29:09-07:00","id":540694,"title":"","content":"@2: We could just substitute the 'Integrity' trait of the supernatural in question. [Humanity (Vampire: The Requiem), Wisdom (Mage: The Awakening), Pilgrimage (Promethean: The Created), Clarity (Changeling: The Lost), Memory (Mummy: The Curse) Cover (Demon: The Descent), Harmony (Werewolf: The Forsaken), Synergy (Geist: The Sin-Eaters), Satiety (Beast: The Primordial)]<br /> <br /> Sure it means that some groups are more prone to Obsessive behaviour. I can live with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T05:56:26-07:00","id":541026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amaterasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/540552-apple-of-discord#post540552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Is the Exceptional Success result really intended/expected to cause a riot upon usage (literal, like dropping Inits as people pull out gun/fang/claw) ? Otherwise how exactly is &quot;must immediately acquire&quot; interpreted?</div> </div> </div> </div> It <i>can</i> cause a riot if used in front of a large number of witnesses. Large groups have the tendency to devolve into the lowest common denominator, thus a mob mentality. However, I would point out that would be kind of obvious, and call for Compromise checks. Remember that Embeds are generally meant to be subtle. Using it in a way that's unsubtle is a great way to peak GM's interest.<br /> <br /> Now, showing the Apple to a small group of people? They'll be less likely to devolve into violence instantly (less chance of lowest common denominator), will still try to get it asap, but they won't be dumb about it. They will know that killing and assault in front of witnesses will equal jail time and loss of the item. The Apple inflicts Obsession and removes moral compasses, it doesn't make people into violent brutes. <br /> <br /> Immediately, in this case, means they want it as soon as they can, and they'll have full use of their mental and social faculties. One guy may try to just buy the object/person with obscene amounts of money first. The loser may wait until they're alone to stab the guy and take the item. Immediately does not equal attracting attention. <br /> <br /> Remember that the item doesn't send them into a berzerk fever. It just makes them desire it. So, they're willing to do whatever it takes, but they're not going to be dumb about it and metaphorically shoot themselves in the foot. They'll generally be smart. Remember, designed to be subtle. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Using Integrity as the Resistance implies non-Mortals are not affected by this power at all (Demons do not have Integrity or any analogous stat, Vampires' Humanity is similar but represents something very different, and Werewolves' Harmony also doesn't map to Integrity in any way whatsoever). Is that how others interpret it, is that the intended implication, or do most just throw whatever Integrity-replacement in that roll (which makes no sense for Demons' Cover rating)? </div> </div> </div> Generally speaking, Embeds don't work well against non-mortals very well. I wouldn't be surprised if the intent was just targeting mortals and not other supernaturals. I notice that DtD games tend to assume that you're dealing with mooks instead of angels on a day-to-day basis. In general, I'm not a fan of how Embeds are designed - they're basically the magical equivalent of Down and Dirty fighting. While appropriate for humans, they're badly designed for use against someone of note, especially fellow PCs or major NPCs.<br /> <br /> Mechanically speaking, substituting out one Integrity system for the nearest equivalent is generally how things work. That said, I would go with restricting it to mortals, primarily because I don't think its use on fellow Unchained or Angels would make sense. Far too powerful of a bargaining chip in any pact or deal, and the power effectively lasts forever, so they'll feel its a good bargain for a bag of junk. I'm not even going to start on how inappropriate it is to use on an Angel. Exceptional Success, fall achieved! Yeah, no. <br /> <br /> <br /> If players want to use it on other supernaturals, I'd go by a case-by-case basis (as dramatically appropriate), and almost certainly include the power stat as part of the resistance, since we're talking about","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T18:26:22-07:00","id":541930,"title":"","content":"Others have suggested solid options for handling it at the table. As always, rule it as you feel best fits your game.<br /> <br /> That said, I wrote it under the (now proven incorrect) understanding that &quot;Integrity&quot; would be a broad category into which other so-called morality stats would fall rather than something specific to mortals. So I intended for it to be usable on other supernatural creatures, but I can see how that doesn't come across. Additionally, I didn't own Werewolf at the time and so didn't realize Harmony was best when it is in balance rather than at the extreme upper end. So you may indeed want to do things like factor power stats into resistance.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}